# CONTEXT FILE — YM Sisters National Finance Quarter Reports

> **Purpose of this file:** Master context for generating the Young Muslims National Finance Report. 
> Feed this file to Claude assistant when drafting the report.
> Anything marked `[DATA NEEDED]` or `[TBD]` must be filled in before generation, or the generator should insert a clearly-marked placeholder.

---

## 1. Output Specification

- **Deliverable:** A polished, print-ready **PDF** hosted on the YM Sisters website via an html file uploaded to the site.
- **Recommended workflow:** Build as a single-file **HTML page**
- **Length target:** ~10–15 pages.
- **Page furniture:** Cover page → Bismillah SVG → table of contents → numbered sections (01, 02, 03… matching handbook convention) → closing/footer: "Young Muslims Sisters · Finance Department · finance@ymsisters.com · [QX] [FYxxxx] National Finance Report · For Internal Use Only".
- **Reporting period:** `[QX FYxxxx]` — specify the exact months included (e.g., Q1 = Jan–Mar, Q2 = Apr–Jun, Q3 = Jul–Sep, Q4 = Oct–Dec).

## 2. Audience & Tone

- **Audience:** YM National Shura (NS), YM National Department teams, SubRegional Coordinators (SRCs) and their SubRegional Shuras, and NeighborNet Coordinators (NNCs) and their NeighborNet Shuras across 170+ chapters.
- **Tone:** Professional but warm and community-oriented. Celebrate wins, be transparent about numbers, be firm-but-friendly on policy reminders. Mirror the handbooks' voice: direct rules softened with helpful explanation.
- **Islamic framing:** Open with Bismillah. Honorifics: Allah ﷻ, the Messenger ﷺ. Include intro and closing duaas

## 3. Glossary / Terminology (use consistently)

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| YM | Young Muslims (the national organization) |
| YMS | Young Muslims Sisters (YMS is the sisters branch of the organization) |
| NN | NeighborNet — a local chapter in YM |
| SR | SubRegion — a grouping of NNs in an area|
| NC | National Coordinator — the amir (leader) of the National Shura |
| NS | National Shura — national leadership council (shura is the term used) - there is a representative from nearly every SubRegion|
| NNC | NeighborNet Coordinator - the amir (leader) of the NeighborNet and its shura |
| SRC | SubRegional Coordinator - the amir (leader) of the Subregion and its shura |
| YMC | YM Conference — national conferences at ICNA-MAS Conference, main YMC is held in ICNA-MAS Conference in Baltimore, but there are smaller ones held in the South (TX), West (California), and Southeast (Georgia) |
| YMLC | YM Leadership Conference - event happens in Q3 but **finances start to hit in Q2**, this is a weekend retreat for all leadership in the country to attend for workshops, networking, and suhbah. The location of this conference changes each year. |
| MAD | Muslim Advocacy Day — advocacy event that YM attends in Washington, D.C. |
| YM Gives | National service campaign run across NNs |
| JotForm | The single intake form for all income/expense/transfer submissions |
| Dashboard | Per-NN/SR/National team finance dashboard spreadsheets refreshed from JotForm data |
| YM Bank | Chapter funds that belong to an NN/SR/National Team that are held by YM National (not physically with the NN/SR/National Team) - kinda like a checking account for NNs, SRs, and National Teams|
| Cash Box | NN's local physical cash (≤ $200 at any time) |
| Personal Bank | NNC's personal account temporarily holding YM funds |

