### 5.3 [QX] National Initiatives
One card per initiative active this quarter. Cards are not purely financial — include participation/operational stats where available, and financials where relevant.

**Card format for each initiative:**
- Tag label (e.g., YMC, YMLC, MAD, YM Gives)
- Event name + location
- 1-sentence description
- Stat trio: mix of participation stats (attendees, sessions, NNs) and financial stats (income, expenses) — use whichever tells the story best
- ⚠️ If a future-quarter event has costs hitting this quarter (e.g., YMLC deposits in Q2), note it explicitly on the card: "these are advance payments; the event takes place in [QX+1]"

**Common initiatives by quarter** (include only those active):
- **YMC — YM Conference** (Baltimore, typically Q2): Registration income + total expenses. Note if hotel/bus costs are pass-throughs.
- **YMLC — YM Leadership Conference** (takes place Q3, but Q2 expenses are deposits/advance payments): Attendees, sessions, speakers + Q2 total expenses. `[DATA NEEDED]`
- **MAD — Muslim Advocacy Day** (D.C., typically Q2): Attendees + states represented. `[DATA NEEDED]`
- **YM Gives** (national service campaign, timing varies): NNs participating. `[DATA NEEDED]`
- **NER — NorthEast Retreat** or other regional retreats if applicable. `[DATA NEEDED if active]`

End this section with a **"Sisterhood in action" photo gallery** — 2–4 photos from events this quarter, each with a caption (`Event · NN/SR · Month`). `[DATA NEEDED: photos]`

